<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Austerlitz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1805">1805</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Battle of the Three Emperors · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-third-coalition">War of the Third Coalition</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Austerlitz was fought on 2 December 1805 near Austerlitz (Slavkov u Brna) in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a>, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-third-coalition">War of the Third Coalition</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s French army decisively defeated the Russian and Austrian armies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-i-of-russia">Alexander I</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii">Emperor Francis II</a>. The victory forced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> to accept the Peace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bratislava">Pressburg</a>, led to the dissolution of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>, and is often counted as Napoleon's greatest triumph.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-austerlitz.jpg" alt="Battle of Austerlitz" width="320" height="159" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: François Gérard · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:La_bataille_d%27Austerlitz._2_decembre_1805_(Fran%C3%A7ois_G%C3%A9rard).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Defeat by Napoleon at the <b>Battle of Austerlitz</b> in December 1805 and the Peace of Pressburg cost Austria Tyrol, Vorarlberg and Venetia, and the formation of the Confederation of the Rhine in July 1806 made the old empire meaningless.</blockquote><a href="/empire/austrian-empire">Austrian Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>After the defeat at <b>Austerlitz</b> and the formation of the Confederation of the Rhine, he dissolved the Holy Roman Empire on 6 August 1806.</blockquote><a href="/empire/habsburg-monarchy">Habsburg Monarchy · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Frederick the Great's siege of Olomouc failed in 1758, Napoleon won the <b>Battle of Austerlitz</b> near Brno in 1805, and in 1866 Prussian troops occupied Brno before the preliminary peace of the Austro-Prussian War was signed at Mikulov (Nikolsburg).</blockquote><a href="/empire/margraviate-of-moravia">Margraviate of Moravia · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The '<b>Battle of the Three Emperors</b>' knocked Austria out of the Third Coalition.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/december-2">2 December in history</a></li><li><blockquote>After Austria's defeat at <b>Austerlitz</b>, the Peace of Pressburg in December 1805 gave Salzburg to the Austrian Empire, and Ferdinand was compensated with Würzburg.</blockquote><a href="/state/electorate-of-salzburg">Electorate of Salzburg</a></li><li><blockquote>He allied with Napoleon in 1805 and sent troops to the <b>Austerlitz</b> campaign.</blockquote><a href="/state/electorate-of-wurttemberg">Electorate of Württemberg</a></li></ul></section>
